### Secrets ###
# application.properties is no longer ignored: every credential in it has been
# replaced by a ${ENV_VAR} placeholder, so the file is now safe - and necessary -
# to commit. Previously it was excluded precisely because it held a database
# password, a JWT signing secret and a block of AWS RDS credentials. If you
# re-add a literal secret to it, this line needs to come back.
#   src/main/resources/application.properties

# Real values live here instead. Commit .env.example, never .env.
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local

# Uploaded product images are user data, not source. These were being committed.
images/
